BT /F1 8.70 Tf 44.00 490.19 Td (The MARS platform is a collection of lightweight mobile robotic agents intended to support research and experimentation) Tj ET
0.200 0.250 0.330 rg
BT /F1 8.70 Tf 44.00 478.99 Td (in multi-agent robotic systems.) Tj ET
0.200 0.250 0.330 rg
BT /F1 8.70 Tf 44.00 464.79 Td (Each robot is an independent physical unit with its own onboard computational, sensing, actuation, and communication) Tj ET
0.200 0.250 0.330 rg
BT /F1 8.70 Tf 44.00 453.59 Td (capabilities.) Tj ET
0.200 0.250 0.330 rg
BT /F1 8.70 Tf 44.00 439.39 Td (Robots may operate individually or cooperate with other robots to accomplish shared objectives.) Tj ET
0.200 0.250 0.330 rg
BT /F1 8.70 Tf 44.00 425.19 Td (The platform additionally supports physical robot-to-robot connection, allowing multiple independent robotic agents to) Tj ET
0.200 0.250 0.330 rg
BT /F1 8.70 Tf 44.00 413.99 Td (form a larger composite robotic configuration.) Tj ET
0.200 0.250 0.330 rg
BT /F1 8.70 Tf 44.00 399.79 Td (Depending on the experiment, connected robots may coordinate their actions while retaining their individual computational) Tj ET
0.200 0.250 0.330 rg
BT /F1 8.70 Tf 44.00 388.59 Td (identities.) Tj ET
0.200 0.250 0.330 rg
BT /F1 8.70 Tf 44.00 374.39 Td (The platform is intended to support both manually controlled and autonomous operation, with centralized supervision and) Tj ET
0.200 0.250 0.330 rg
BT /F1 8.70 Tf 44.00 363.19 Td (decentralized coordination available according to the experimental requirements.) Tj ET
